The original [incident page](/kb/incidents/4471/) says one issue and one queued fix.
The exported data and the KB's running classification separate two problems. Fixing
the shared parser does not establish that the booking form's hint is correct.

## Distinct reports and causes

<IncidentSummary />

These counts describe the export dated 4 October 2026. They are computed at render
time from the reports and tenant directory, using `uniqueById`, `causeOf` and
`groupByCause`. They do not claim to represent later changes at the desk.

## Parser problem

[GitHub issue: shared parser](https://github.com/brendanshean/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1).

The shared parser reads every date month first. Day-first tenants supplying dates
through the app, email or the older booking form can therefore have the month and
day reversed. For example, report R-41200 from harbour.dental describes a 7 April
reminder going out on 4 July. Its tenant locale is en-GB.

The parser should interpret a date using the applicable tenant's format, or accept
an unambiguous date representation. Verify both an ambiguous date and a day above
12, and preserve correct behavior for month-first tenants. These are proposed
acceptance checks; the production parser is not included in this KB export.

## Form-hint problem

[GitHub issue: booking-v3 hint](https://github.com/brendanshean/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2).

For a day-first tenant on booking-v3, the form displays `MM/DD/YYYY` while interpreting
the entry in the tenant's day-first order. A person following the hint can therefore
submit a different date. This affects form reports from alder.physio, copper.studio
and pale.harbour in this export.

For example, R-41230 is a copper.studio form report about 6 January becoming 1 June.
It was tagged `parser` at intake, but the tenant and form classify it as `hint`.
The hint and input interpretation must agree. Verify booking-v3 for day-first and
month-first tenants, and confirm that the fix also preserves booking-v2 behavior.

